[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3927965702","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116257#issuecomment-3927965702","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116257","id":3927965702,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qIAAG","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-19T15:23:51Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T15:27:25Z","body":"@jrouwe might correct me here, but I believe this is largely the expected behavior, as CCD in either engine does not take angular velocity into account, since it's implemented using a linear shape-cast in both. I believe the only real workaround in this case would be to crank up the `physics/common/physics_ticks_per_second` project setting.\n\nI guess the question is whether this is the only possible way to implement CCD, or if there's some other approach that would take angular velocity into account, but this probably shouldn't be framed as a bug in either case.\n\nIt does seem like something worth mentioning in the documentation of the `continuous_cd` property though. It's not the first time I've seen this reported.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3927965702/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3928796699","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116257#issuecomment-3928796699","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116257","id":3928796699,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qLK4b","user":{"login":"GorgWorgington","id":9775975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3NzU5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9775975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington","html_url":"https://github.com/GorgWorgington","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-19T17:39:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T17:39:48Z","body":"Something that bears mentioning is the fact that so far it only seems to happen with trimesh collision shapes. In the MRP scene I included there is another StaticBody3D with a box collision shape you can enable to see this. Either way, the level of clipping that my team is experiencing in our game is extreme and the velocities involved aren't even very big.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3928796699/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3928854719","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116257#issuecomment-3928854719","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116257","id":3928854719,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qLZC_","user":{"login":"GorgWorgington","id":9775975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3NzU5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9775975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington","html_url":"https://github.com/GorgWorgington","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-19T17:47:57Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T17:47:57Z","body":"Setting `physics/common/physics_ticks_per_second` to a higher value in the MRP seems to mitigate it but even setting it as high as 120 only seems to be a bandaid. Even without CCD I would expect there to be no clipping.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3928854719/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3928961662","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116257#issuecomment-3928961662","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116257","id":3928961662,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qLzJ-","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-19T18:06:55Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T18:06:55Z","body":"> Something that bears mentioning is the fact that so far it only seems to happen with trimesh collision shapes.\n\n`ConcavePolygonShape3D` are hollow, whereas convex shapes (like `BoxShape3D`) are not, even when it's an enclosed shape like yours is. It's perfectly valid for something to be inside of it, so it doesn't take much for a thin object like your `Board` to end up far enough on the other side of a triangle for the collision to be resolved inwards instead.\n\nIf you need more complex collision geometry without resorting to `ConcavePolygonShape3D` you have convex decomposition available in Godot, using \"Mesh\" > \"Create Collision Shape\" > \"Multiple Convex\" in the viewport toolbar menu, when selecting a `MeshInstance3D`.\n\nYou can also have Godot do this automatically when importing a mesh, [like so](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/assets_pipeline/importing_3d_scenes/node_type_customization.html#create-collisions-col-convcol-colonly-convcolonly).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3928961662/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3929028001","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116257#issuecomment-3929028001","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116257","id":3929028001,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qMDWh","user":{"login":"GorgWorgington","id":9775975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3NzU5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9775975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington","html_url":"https://github.com/GorgWorgington","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-19T18:19:20Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T18:19:20Z","body":"I see. Unfortunately it seems that convex decomposition is bugged and produces inaccurate shapes, but that's another issue (#29971). Thank you for providing your insight.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3929028001/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3940662526","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116257#issuecomment-3940662526","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116257","id":3940662526,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7q4bz-","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-22T10:26:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-22T10:26:25Z","body":"Everything @mihe says is correct.\n\n> I guess the question is whether this is the only possible way to implement CCD, or if there's some other approach that would take angular velocity into account, but this probably shouldn't be framed as a bug in either case.\n\nIt is possible to implement CCD that takes angular velocity into account. This is something I want to add to Jolt in the future (it's why `EMotionQuality` is an enum and not a bool), but I've not done any serious investigation into it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3940662526/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3940676108","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116257#issuecomment-3940676108","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116257","id":3940676108,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7q4fIM","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-22T10:35:27Z","updated_at":"2026-02-22T10:35:27Z","body":"I'll go ahead and reframe this as a documentation issue, and we can close this once we've added a mention of this gotcha to the `RigidBody3D.continuous_cd` property.\n\nAny requests for improvements to CCD would be better suited for [godotengine/godot-proposals](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals), or Jolt's own GitHub repository perhaps.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3940676108/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]